+# Jenkins pipeline inventory — the pipeline types, and how the files handle each guide topic
+
+Built 2026-09-30 by slice 034 (phase P4, requirement R1). The style guide takes one reference
+Jenkinsfile per type below, and the migration slice after it works from this page. Sources:
+
+- `files.tsv`, regenerated with `analyse.py` after a fresh fetch of every clone. The only change
+  since the 09-30 refresh is `KubeCoder/Jenkinsfile`, declarative since slice 033 (408 lines).
+- The Jenkins job list, read through the API on 2026-09-30. It is the same 124 jobs as
+  [Appendix A](report.md#appendix-a--ans-84-move-inventory).
+- Every in-scope Jenkinsfile, read on the branch its job builds (`origin/<branch>` in the clones
+  under `/work/scratch`). Line numbers are that day's.
+
+**Scope.** Appendix A has 124 jobs. The ten jobs of the five ModernAppTemplate repos are skipped
+(next section). Each of the other 114 belongs to exactly one of the 13 types, and only those 114
+count toward the variants under each topic. To rebuild the state, see "State does not survive an
+environment" in [plan.md](plan.md).
+
+## Skipped: the ModernAppTemplate repos (ruling F2)
+
+The operator, in slice 034's plan review (2026-09-30): "Please completely skip the
+moderapptemplate repos. I'll get them fixed when we do the next sync." DHCPApp,
+ElectronicsInventory, IoTSupport, ZigbeeControl and FieldnotesApp render their `Jenkinsfile` from
+ModernAppTemplate's root template. The ruling skips the repos completely, so their producer jobs
+are skipped as well. None of the ten has a type, and none counts toward a topic's variants.
+
+| Jenkins job | Jenkinsfile |
+|---|---|
+| AaC/DHCPApp | DHCPApp/Jenkinsfile.architecture |
+| AaC/ElectronicsInventory | ElectronicsInventory/Jenkinsfile.architecture |
+| AaC/FieldnotesApp | FieldnotesApp/Jenkinsfile.architecture |
+| AaC/IoTSupport | IoTSupport/Jenkinsfile.architecture |
+| AaC/ZigbeeControl | ZigbeeControl/Jenkinsfile.architecture |
+| DHCP/DHCPApp | DHCPApp/Jenkinsfile |
+| ElectronicsInventory/ElectronicsInventory | ElectronicsInventory/Jenkinsfile |
+| FieldnotesApp | FieldnotesApp/Jenkinsfile |
+| IoTSupport/IoTSupport | IoTSupport/Jenkinsfile |
+| ZigbeeControl/ZigbeeControl | ZigbeeControl/Jenkinsfile |
+
+Three consequences for the rest of this page:
+
+- Every open **A** concurrency candidate in Appendix A is one of these repos.
+- The J11 exception candidates at 90 minutes (ElectronicsInventory, IoTSupport) are skipped.
+- The only in-scope users of the global `KEYCLOAK_*` variables were IoTSupport's two files, so
+  none is left in scope.
+
+## The types
+
+| Type | What the pipeline does | Jobs | Accepted library helper |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| T1 | App architecture producer: validates the repo's hand-authored architecture YAML and archives it | 23 | J16 |
+| T2 | Deploy-repo architecture producer: generates the YAML from the chart, then validates and archives it | 49 | J16 |
+| T3 | Image build: kaniko image(s), then the image pin written into a deploy repo | 16 | — |
+| T4 | Artifact build for a downstream job: an apk, jar, zip or binary, archived and handed on | 5 | — |
+| T5 | ESP-IDF firmware: builds the firmware and uploads it to the devices over the air | 8 | J14 |
+| T6 | Validation Job: runs the suite as a Kubernetes Job, then builds and pins the image | 1 | J15 |
+| T7 | iac-controller job: declarative, on srviac, every step an `iac` call | 6 | J19, ruled against |
+| T8 | Configuration apply: lints and tests a configuration, then applies it to a live service | 1 | — |
+| T9 | Promotion: hand-started, retags images and advances a deploy branch | 1 | — |
+| T10 | Image matrix: a stage per image variant, generated at run time | 1 | — |
+| T11 | Architecture collector: triggers computed from YAML, collects every producer, builds the viewer | 1 | — |
+| T12 | Scheduled snapshot producer: a producer artifact generated from a live system on a cron | 1 | — |
+| T13 | Kiosk cross-build with an SSH deploy; the job is disabled | 1 | — |
+| | | **114** | |
+
+### T1 — App architecture producer (23)
+
+Each is a `<Repo>/Jenkinsfile.architecture` run by job `AaC/<Repo>`. The pod inherits
+`jenkins-agent` and adds `containerTemplates.aac_tools('aac-tools')`. Stage `Cloning repo` runs
+`checkout scm`. Stage `Architecture` runs `arch-validate docs/architecture/*.yaml` in `aac-tools`,
+then `archiveArtifacts`. With comments stripped, 21 files are one body.
+
+Members: AaC/Ansible, AaC/CalendarDisplay, AaC/DockerImages, AaC/DoorbellReceiver,
+AaC/GestureDevice, AaC/Ginbov, AaC/GitblitMCPServer, AaC/GitblitMCPSupportPlugin,
+AaC/InfraStatisticsDisplay, AaC/Intercom, AaC/IntercomServer, AaC/KitchenDisplay, AaC/KubeCoder,
+AaC/MyDownloadsClient, AaC/MyDownloadsServer, AaC/NewsFilter, AaC/PaperClock, AaC/SSEGateway,
+AaC/ScanToPdfClient, AaC/ScanToPdfServer, AaC/UnderfloorHeatingController, AaC/Webathome,
+AaC/YouTrackMCPServer.
+
+- **AaC/Ansible** validates one named file (`docs/architecture/ansible-architecture.yaml`), in a
+  stage of its own, and archives in another. It inherits `jenkins-agent kaniko` without building
+  an image, and it has no header comment.
+- **AaC/DockerImages** copies each `*/architecture.yaml` to `docs/architecture/<app>.yaml` before
+  it validates (`:28-35`). It clones itself with `git` (`:19-21`).
+- **Header comments.** Two wordings are shared. One is in 12 files: the device and client/server
+  repos. The other is in 8: Ginbov, the Gitblit pair, MyDownloadsServer, NewsFilter, SSEGateway,
+  Webathome and YouTrackMCPServer. AaC/KubeCoder and AaC/DockerImages each have a header of their
+  own, and AaC/Ansible has none.
+
