+### post and notify
+
+- **No pod pipeline has a `post` block or calls `notify`.** For them the bot's FAILURE report is
+  the only alert: an ABORTED or UNSTABLE build is posted silently.
+- **T7 pages a failed dev stage in two ways** (J19's "two variants of the paging rule"):
+  - IaC/Apply, Calico and Update set `env.DEV_STAGE_FAILED = 'true'` and call `unstable(…)` in
+    the stage. Their `post { unstable { script { if (env.DEV_STAGE_FAILED == 'true')
+    notify.warning(…) } } }` then pages.
+  - Certs and Drift call `notify.warning(message)` and then `unstable(message)` in the stage
+    itself.
+  - IaC/Build-Main has no `post` block and says why (`:93-95`).
+- **No file has `post { aborted }`.**
+- **`catchError(buildResult: 'FAILURE', stageResult: 'FAILURE')`** in Certs' `prdStage` (`:76`)
+  and Drift's `prdCheck` (`:172`) records a prd failure and lets the later stages run.
+- **`currentBuild.description`** carries a summary in Certs, Drift (the drift summary),
+  Promote-PRD and SSEGateway (the test counts).
+- SSEGateway deletes its Job in `try { … } finally { kubectl.deleteJob(…) }`.
